x-p-800.jpg 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x-p-1080.jpg 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x-p-1600.jpg 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x.jpg 2400w\" class=\"cms-card_image w-condition-invisible\"><img src=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" sizes=\"100vw\" srcset=\"https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x-p-500.jpg 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x-p-800.jpg 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x-p-1080.jpg 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x-p-1600.jpg 1600w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6568a1bce0ae49e6bedec3a6/69e0fac138328bc98e480bd3_Halcyon-blog-hero-RRC-alert-automotive-industry-1200x630%402x.jpg 2400w\" class=\"cms-card_image\"></div></div><div class=\"cms-card_meta-wrapper\"><div fs-cmsfilter-field=\"date\" class=\"text-style-date text-color-blue\">Apr 15, 2026</div><div class=\"category-link is-outline\"><div fs-cmsfilter-field=\"category\">Research</div></div></div><div class=\"cms-card_title-link\"><h3 fs-cmsfilter-field=\"title\" class=\"heading-style-cms-card\">44% and Rising: What the Automotive Industry's Ransomware Problem Tells Us About Where Attacks Are Heading</h3></div><div class=\"cms-card_description\"><p fs-cmsfilter-field=\"description\" class=\"text-size-small truncate\">Automotive ransomware attacks doubled in 2025, reaching 44% of all reported incidents. Groups like BlackSuit, Qilin, and Akira are running coordinated campaigns against OEMs and suppliers, with supply chain compromises cascading across thousands of downstream victims.</p></div><div class=\"cms-card_button-wrapper\"><div data-w-id=\"7c0c7317-1185-f172-f55b-212e80f113ec\" class=\"button-secondary\"><div>Read the Blog</div><div class=\"button-secondary-icon-wrap\"><div data-w-id=\"7c0c7317-1185-f172-f55b-212e80f113ef\" style=\"transform: translate3d(0px, 0px, 0px) scale3d(1, 1, 1) rotateX(0deg) rotateY(0deg) rotateZ(0deg) skew(0deg); transform-style: preserve-3d;\" class=\"button-secondary-icon w-embed\"><svg width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n<path d=\"M1.00066 6.00001H10.3563M10.3563 6.00001L5.67847 10.6778M10.3563 6.00001L5.67847 1.32221\" stroke=\"currentcolor\" stroke-width=\"1.34566\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"></path>\n</svg></div><div data-w-id=\"7c0c7317-1185-f172-f55b-212e80f113f0\" style=\"transform: translate3d(-30px, 0px, 0px) scale3d(1, 1, 1) rotateX(0deg) rotateY(0deg) rotateZ(0deg) skew(0deg); transform-style: preserve-3d;\" class=\"button-secondary-icon is-absolute w-embed\"><svg width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n<path d=\"M1.00066 6.00001H10.3563M10.3563 6.00001L5.67847 10.6778M10.3563 6.00001L5.67847 1.32221\" stroke=\"currentcolor\" stroke-width=\"1.34566\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"></path>\n</svg></div></div></div></div></a>","link":"https://www.halcyon.ai/blog/44-percent-and-rising-automotive-ransomware","retrieved":1776211200000},{"title":"What Mythos Actually Changes About Ransom